meta {
  name: Reject - unknown API path
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/nonexistent
  body: none
  auth: none
}

tests {
  test("answers JSON, not the HTML page the short domain serves", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(404);
    expect(res.body.error.code).to.equal("not_found");
  });

  test("does not demand a token before admitting the path does not exist", function () {
    expect(res.body.error.code).to.not.equal("unauthenticated");
  });
}

docs {
  The other half of the catch-all. Everything under `/api` that no route claims
  answers in the standard error envelope, because a client that parses JSON can
  do nothing with a page about short links.

  Deliberately unauthenticated: demanding a token before admitting a path does
  not exist reports a typo as `unauthenticated`, which sends whoever made it
  looking at their credentials instead of at their URL.
}
